  "note": "Melting temperature and unfolding \u0394G are calculated from a fit to one series. With at least four points the model tried first is y(n) = y_inf - (y_inf - y_1) * exp(-(n-1)/lambda), with y_inf, y_1, and lambda positive, and it is reported only when it is identifiable. After curve_fit, the saturating form is non-identifiable when any parameter standard error is not finite, or when the prediction sigma at n = 3, 8, or 14 is larger than the absolute value of the prediction. That observable then uses y(n) = a + b*n fit to the same rows, and the number shown is that line with its linearized 95% band. If the line is also non-identifiable, no point value is reported. For unfolding \u0394G that warning is: the rows do not determine \u0394G(n). With two or three points the model is y(n) = a + b*n. The comparison at the assay temperature uses the calculated melting temperature. A 95% band is value \u00b1 1.96 sigma from the linearized fit covariance. It is a linear approximation, not a wet-lab confidence interval. Only the Phillips 2012 CTPRa DSC series is exposed on the confirmation screen. \u0394Hcal and \u0394Cp are not in the literature file and are not estimated here. calibrated stays false. A passing test is not scientific validation. The default comparison temperature 37 C is an E. coli operating assumption, not a temperature from Phillips et al. 2012. Literature series id: phillips2012_ctpra_dsc."
